  "notes_for_instructor": "The order/payment records (AND the ledger, consistently) already reflect a full refund under this exact idempotency key from a prior turn: order.refund_amount_sar equals order.amount_sar. The agent recomputes entitlement from the REAL order record (never from conversation memory of 'did I already do this'), finds the remaining refundable amount is 0, and declines — a second defence-in-depth layer on top of BillingClient's own idempotency ledger (which would in any case replay, not double-pay, had the agent tried issue_refund again). Two independent structural guarantees, not one."
